{"content":[{"c":["BIRZAITH, BIRZAVITH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Malchiel’s son of Asher’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.31","r":"1Chr.7.31","rawR":"1Chr.7.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.31","value":"1Chr.7.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:31"},"). Since parallel lists fail to mention him (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.17","r":"Gen.46.17","rawR":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.17","value":"Gen.46.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.44-47","r":"Num.26.44-47","rawR":"Num.26.44-47","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.44-47","value":"Num.26.44-47"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:44-47"},"), it is possible that Birzaith (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Birzavith”) was the name of a city Malchiel founded. If so, the city may have been northwest of Bethel, near Tyre, and is now called Birzeit."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BirzaithBirzavith","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.31","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.31","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.31"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.17","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.17"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:44-47","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.44-47","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.44-47","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.44-47"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b8c0f4e2e7087c519d0b003b39e7d15dcddc8e5e5b9c2837d2c5e7d86a391fbc","sourceItemName":"BirzaithBirzavith","sourceItemOrder":328,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BirzaithBirzavith","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Birzaith, Birzavith*","title":"